WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.834
-Republicans immediately started

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.234
attacking President Biden
for high gas prices

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:07.667
after he announced a ban
on Russian energy imports,

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:10.000
while Ukrainian
President Volodymyr Zelensky

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.334
bravely defied
an increasingly isolated

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:13.701
and desperate Vladimir Putin.

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:15.934
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:20.467
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.033
Authoritarian regimes depend

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.901
on stifling the flow
of information

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:25.567
and creating alternate realities

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.133
and that can even apply
to the autocrats themselves.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:31.467
In fact, dictators often occupy
their own alternate realities,

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.834
which seems to be what's
happening with Vladimir Putin.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:35.534
He's the only person
in the world who seems

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:38.467
to think this is a good idea,
this horrific war,

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.801
and he's increasingly isolated
from outside voices,

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.000
both figuratively and literally.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.434
He makes even his
highest-ranking officials sit

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:46.734
at the other end of a giant room

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:47.901
[ Laughter ]
in televised meetings and,

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.334
even when they sit
at the same table,

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:51.801
he chooses the longest table
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.300
he can possibly find.
I mean, what's that about?

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.901
It looks like he's playing
shuffleboard in a college bar.

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:58.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.667
Next, he's going
to make them meet

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.434
in the pods
from "Love Is Blind."

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:03.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:04.934
[ Russian accent ]
Vlad, why are you upset?

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:07.501
Both Jessica and Lisa said
you are their number one.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.534
[ As Putin ]
Yes, but I cannot tell

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.234
if they said that
because they like me

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.234
or because they are required
to say it by law.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:16.367
The point is
Putin is clearly isolated,

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:17.601
even from his top officials.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.534
In fact, Ukrainian
President Volodymyr Zelensky

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.567
is defying Putin
by doing the exact opposite.

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.667
He posted a video of himself
in his office,

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.534
revealing his location
earlier this week,

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:27.868
despite the fact
that Putin is after him.

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:30.767
-Just moments ago, Ukrainian
President Volodymyr Zelensky

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.334
posted this video on Facebook.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:35.667
It's the first time he's been
seen in his official office

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.267
since Russia
invaded his country,

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:40.501
Zelensky saying,
at the top of the video,

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:43.200
"I'm staying in Kyiv,
in my office.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.267
I'm not hiding
and I'm not afraid of anyone."

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.901
-Damn, that is incredibly brave.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.834
I don't even let
our cue card guy, Wally,

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:52.467
you know where I am
until the show starts.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.300
[ Laughter ]
He's always trying to get me

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.200
to invest in his new line
of Wallmark greeting cards.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.968
[ Laughter ]
-Seth, we have cards

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:02.601
for every occasion --
birthdays, holidays.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.801
-No one wants to invest
in this idea!

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.667
-Why?
-The cards are too big!

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.200
-We provide the envelope.
-We will have this
conversation later!

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:11.767
-Sounds like someone just went

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:13.167
from a no to a maybe.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.200
[ Laughter ]
-Wally!

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.734
Anyway, Putin, very clearly,
is living in a bubble

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.067
and he wants everyone else
to join him in that bubble.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.834
His regime has been cracking
down on independent media,

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:26.801
rounding up protesters
by the thousands,

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.868
and passed a law
making it illegal

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:31.234
to call Russia's invasion
of Ukraine a war.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:32.901
-Tonight, inside Russia,

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:35.934
the president signing a new law
passed by parliament,

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:37.801
making it illegal to distribute

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:41.901
so-called false information
about the military operation.

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.501
Calling the operation
in Ukraine

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:47.234
an invasion or a war
could be illegal.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:51.367
Breaking the law could result
in up to 15 years in prison.

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:53.467
-That's right, they're not even
allowed to call it

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:54.968
a war or invasion anymore.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:57.601
In fact, the list
of Kremlin-approved
phrases includes...

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:04.133
...and, of course...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:07.434
So Putin is isolated, unhinged,
and disconnected from reality,

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:08.968
if he thinks it's going
to end well.

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.567
The Russian economy
is being squeezed

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.133
by intense
international sanctions

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:15.000
and the global condemnation has
been swift and all-encompassing.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.434
Russia's essentially
been cut off

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.133
from the global
financial system.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:20.701
Russian oligarchs are having
their yachts and villas seized,

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.400
major American companies
are suspending

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.367
their business in Russia
and, on top of all that,

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.000
President Biden
announced yesterday

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.000
that the U.S. would ban
all Russian energy imports,

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.234
which might make this a good
time to pause and acknowledge

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:33.834
how insane it is
that we continue to buy oil

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.300
from brutal regimes,
like Russia and Saudi Arabia,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.167
as Democratic
Senator Chris Murphy

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:39.234
pointed out yesterday.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.567
-Let's just admit the insanity

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:44.367
of a U.S. economy
that continues to run

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.834
on oil that is provided to us
by dictators.

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:50.267
The reality is, if we're not
getting this oil from Russia,

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:52.167
we're likely going
to be importing more

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:55.701
from another brutal dictator --
in Saudi Arabia, for instance.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.601
Or we may have to go
to Venezuela for oil.

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:59.734
We should ultimately learn
our lesson here

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:03.033
and become energy-independent
and choose to invest

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:06.267
in clean domestic energy,
so we never have to choose

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:08.501
between one dictator
versus another.

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:09.834
-Yeah, I mean,
wouldn't it be nice

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.801
if we could generate
our own clean energy

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.801
through renewable sources,
like wind and solar,

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:16.467
instead of begging murderous
crazy people not to gouge us?

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:18.200
Then, at least,
we'd never have to watch

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.767
another U.S. president
hold a weird, glowing orb

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:23.300
and do a sword dance
with Saudi royals,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.701
[ Laughter ]
like he's auditioning

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:27.534
for a non-flipping role
in Cirque du Soleil.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:29.734
[ Laughter ]
I will give them credit
for one thing --

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:31.634
they found a way to make Trump
look even dumber

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:34.167
than he normally looks,
just bobbing his head,
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:36.868
wagging around a limp sword
like a wet pool noodle.

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:37.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.133
They should just keep giving him

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:40.434
increasingly stupid tasks

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:41.467
and telling him he had to do it

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:42.868
to please
the Saudi royal family.

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.067
"Alright, Mr. President,
and now,

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:45.767
we shall commence
the dance of the butterfly."

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:47.067
[ As Trump ]
Alright, but why am I...

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:48.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:50.767
...why am I the only one
in wings, guys?

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:52.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.601
Living in a world where
we derive our energy

00:04:54.601 --> 00:04:57.167
from clean, renewable sources
would be so much better,

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:58.601
for so many obvious reasons,

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:00.734
including the fact
that it would take power away

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.901
from repressive,
oil-based dictatorships.

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.901
Right now,
they have far too much power

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:06.567
over both global
and domestic politics

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:07.834
because,
as you've probably noticed,

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:09.901
gas prices hit a record high
this week.

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:10.968
The numbers are so shocking,

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:14.300
I drove by a station that had...

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.400
...on the sign.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.801
Both Republicans and Democrats
had called on Biden

00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:21.634
to ban Russian energy --
both parties --

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.667
and yet, you probably won't be
shocked to learn

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:26.334
that Republicans also attacked
him for high gas prices,

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:28.167
like Tennessee
Senator Marsha Blackburn,

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:28.868
who tweeted...

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:33.400
That's true.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.801
And, famously,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.300
that was the only
thing happening in 2020.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:41.234
The low gas year,
as we called it.

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:43.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:44.434
I'm just spitballing here,

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:46.801
but maybe low gas prices
had something to do

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:48.801
with the fact that
we were all trapped in our homes

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:49.934
and no one was going anywhere.

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:52.100
Price goes down
when demand goes down.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.868
That's why you can get
a DVD player for like $11 now

00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:57.734
or a Wallmark card for free.

00:05:57.734 --> 00:05:59.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:00.701
Not now!

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:02.200
[ Laughter ]
It's easy to lower gas prices

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.601
when no one is using gas
to commute or travel

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:05.767
or fly on airplanes.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:07.934
That's like presiding
over a zombie apocalypse

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:08.601
and bragging that...

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:11.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.067
But, yeah,
now that you mention it,

00:06:13.067 --> 00:06:14.968
I do remember
when I was fleeing the city

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:17.100
to avoid a highly contagious
respiratory virus

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.033
that decimated the U.S. economy
and trapped everyone

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:20.434
in their homes
without toilet paper,

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:22.000
not knowing if their jobs
would ever come back

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.167
or their families would survive,

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:25.501
looking up at the gas prices
and thinking,

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:27.801
"Wow, $2.17 a gallon."

00:06:27.801 --> 00:06:30.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.267
"Thank you, President Trump."

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:34.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:37.100
Just to clear a few things up,

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.167
Biden has actually
outpaced Trump

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:40.467
in issuing drilling permits,

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:43.033
despite promising to end
new drilling on federal land.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:46.300
Also, it's worth noting that oil
companies profits soared

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.267
to $174 billion in 2021.

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:51.834
Chevron, alone, raked in
over $15 billion

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:53.701
in annual profits
and, in February,

00:06:53.701 --> 00:06:56.300
BP reported its highest profit
in eight years.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.534
Maybe they could use some
of that money

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.734
to lower gas prices,
instead of stock buybacks

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.634
or shooting glossy
commercials full

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:03.234
of healthy-looking sea turtles,

00:07:03.234 --> 00:07:04.734
or, at the very least,

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:06.367
they could pay
for some better programing

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:08.534
on those damn gas station
TV screens.

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:11.133
[ Laughter ]
I mean, what kind of low-rent
TV show agrees

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:13.501
to be shown
on the outside of a gas pump?

00:07:13.501 --> 00:07:15.667
Good evening, I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:16.834
[ Laughter ]
We hope you're
doing well tonight

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:19.200
and, now, we are going
to get to the news.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.868
Damn it!
I forgot we made that deal.

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:24.467
Even worse, when we made it,
they said,

00:07:24.467 --> 00:07:26.567
"We can pay you in gas
or Slim Jims,"

00:07:26.567 --> 00:07:28.667
and I yelled, "Slim Jims!"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.667 --> 00:07:29.901
I mean, I was thinking,
if anything was due

00:07:29.901 --> 00:07:31.767
to have a price hike,
you know...

00:07:31.767 --> 00:07:33.868
[ Laughter ]
At some point, they're going
to run out of Jims.

00:07:33.868 --> 00:07:35.968
[ Laughter ]
So the GOP complaints
about gas prices

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:37.968
are obviously cynical,
hollow politics

00:07:37.968 --> 00:07:40.000
and, by far,
the dumbest example came

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.968
from Colorado Congresswoman
Lauren Boebert

00:07:41.968 --> 00:07:43.234
on Fox News last night,

00:07:43.234 --> 00:07:45.033
when she tried to slam
the Biden administration,

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:47.334
but seemed to lose her
train of thought.

00:07:47.334 --> 00:07:51.067
-Here's Biden's energy policy --
anyone but America.

00:07:51.067 --> 00:07:53.634
OPEC, Venezuela, you name it.

00:07:53.634 --> 00:07:57.801
If it's not American energy,
Joe doesn't want it.

00:07:57.801 --> 00:08:01.501
Jesse, under President Trump,
America became net --

00:08:01.501 --> 00:08:04.667
a net energy exporter
for the first time in decades

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:07.534
and became the world's
number one producer in oil.

00:08:07.534 --> 00:08:11.133
President Trump unleashed
our energy potential.

00:08:11.133 --> 00:08:15.300
So I say we should be relying
on our guys to do the work,

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.534
not OPEC.

00:08:16.534 --> 00:08:18.167
And I don't know who's running

00:08:18.167 --> 00:08:20.234
the federal government,
these days,

00:08:20.234 --> 00:08:25.601
Joe Biden
or Prince John from, uh,

00:08:25.601 --> 00:08:26.634
Prince John.

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.234
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:30.000
You know, Prince John,
from Prince John.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.567 --> 00:08:33.400
In all seriousness --
and I want to be charitable here

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.567
because she's a member
of Congress

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:36.834
and an elected official,
so, even if we disagree,

00:08:36.834 --> 00:08:38.501
I want to engage with her
in good faith --

00:08:38.501 --> 00:08:39.968
here's my sincere
and honest question --

00:08:39.968 --> 00:08:42.033
What the [bleep]
are you talking about?

00:08:42.033 --> 00:08:43.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:43.367 --> 00:08:45.567
That was like when you're
watching a movie with your mom

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:47.667
and she says, "Hey, it's
that guy from 'Goodfellas,'"

00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:50.200
and you say, "Yeah,
we're watching 'Goodfellas.'"

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.801
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.801 --> 00:08:53.133
I mean, just to try
and figure out

00:08:53.133 --> 00:08:55.667
what she might be talking about,
I Googled "Prince John"

00:08:55.667 --> 00:08:58.033
and this was
on the first page of results.

00:08:58.033 --> 00:09:00.200
-This crown gives me a feeling
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.834
of power!

00:09:01.834 --> 00:09:02.968
Power!

00:09:02.968 --> 00:09:05.267
Forgive me a cruel chuckle.

00:09:05.267 --> 00:09:08.367
[ Chuckle ]
Power.

00:09:08.367 --> 00:09:11.634
-In fairness, he is
a political figure, I guess,

00:09:11.634 --> 00:09:14.000
[ Laughter ]
Prince John.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.434
You know, from Prince John.

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:18.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.601
I'm sure,
in an alternate timeline,

00:09:19.601 --> 00:09:20.901
Lauren Boebert isn't
in Congress.

00:09:20.901 --> 00:09:22.567
She's just writing hate mail
to Disney,

00:09:22.567 --> 00:09:24.567
to complain about how rarely
they open the vault.

00:09:24.567 --> 00:09:25.801
[ As Boebert ]
Thanks to Joe Biden,

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:28.167
Cruella can only afford
seventy-eight dalmatians.

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:29.367
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.367 --> 00:09:31.033
This person should not be
an elected official.

00:09:31.033 --> 00:09:32.434
From now on,
instead of calling her

00:09:32.434 --> 00:09:34.300
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert,
I'm just going to call her

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.000
Lauren Boebert
from Lauren Boebert.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.167
As we're seeing play out
in real time now,

00:09:39.167 --> 00:09:42.100
autocracies and dictatorships
depend on stifling the truth,

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.534
which is why Putin is
so desperate

00:09:43.534 --> 00:09:45.234
to crack down
an independent media

00:09:45.234 --> 00:09:47.601
and stay isolated,
even from his closest officials.

00:09:47.601 --> 00:09:50.567
We should be investing in clean,
renewable energy sources,

00:09:50.567 --> 00:09:52.868
so we don't have to buy oil
from dictators anymore.

00:09:52.868 --> 00:09:56.400
You know, from Saudi Arabia
or from Vladimir Putin, or...

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.467
-From, uh, Prince John.

00:09:59.467 --> 00:10:01.467
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:01.467 --> 00:10:05.334
♪♪

00:10:05.334 --> 00:10:06.801
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:10:06.801 --> 00:10:08.100
over two million meals a year

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:10.200
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:11.601
cancer, and other
serious illnesses

00:10:11.601 --> 00:10:13.434
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:10:13.434 --> 00:10:15.567
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:10:15.567 --> 00:10:18.133
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

